{"case_id":"T8035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","configuration","input_semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["simdjson::dom::parser::parse_many","simdjson::dom::parser::load_many","simdjson::dom::document_stream::document_stream","simdjson::dom::document_stream::start","simdjson::dom::document_stream::next","simdjson::dom::document_stream::load_batch","simdjson::internal::simdjson_result_base<T>::tie","simdjson::internal::simdjson_result_base<T>::get","simdjson::simdjson_result<T>::get","simdjson::dom::element::get(T &)","simdjson::simdjson_result<simdjson::dom::element>::get(T &)"],"reason":"H0 only calls single-document parser.parse and never exercises the changed parse_many/document_stream path. It therefore misses multi-document framing, iteration across batch boundaries, fuzz-controlled batch_size, stream error states, and the optional threaded stage-1 state machine. H0 also uses tie(elem, error) only for parse results and never exercises the new error_code-returning get(T &) protocol, including successful assignment, preservation of the destination on error, incorrect-type conversions, and the element::get<element> specialization.","evidence":["Every H0 entry point constructs simdjson::dom::parser and calls parser.parse(...); none calls parser.parse_many, parser.load_many, or iterates simdjson::dom::document_stream.","S1 changes parser::parse_many to construct document_stream(*this, batch_size, buf, len) and splits document_stream construction into a normal buffer constructor and an initial-error constructor.","document_stream exposes stateful start(), next(), load_batch(), next_batch_start(), and run_stage1(), with additional SIMDJSON_THREADS_ENABLED worker and stage1_thread_parser state absent from H0.","S1 changes simdjson_result_base<T>::tie so value is assigned only when error is SUCCESS and adds get(T &) returning error_code.","S1 replaces element::get(T &, error_code &) with error_code element::get(T &) and adds the explicit element::get<element>(element &) specialization; H0 does not call these overloads."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated harness that partitions fuzz bytes into a batch_size and a raw multi-document buffer, calls parser.parse_many, iterates the entire document_stream while consuming both documents and errors, and runs in threaded and non-threaded configurations. Also add operations that invoke get(T &) on parse results and elements for every supported type, checking error propagation and that output values are not consumed on failure."}
